    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `sglang.lang.backend.runtime_endpoint.RuntimeEndpoint._handle_dtype_to_regex`, `sampling_params.stop` is only converted to a list when it equals the default empty tuple `()`:\n```python\nif sampling_params.stop == ():\n    sampling_params.stop = []\n\ndtype_regex = None\nif sampling_params.dtype in [\"int\", int]:\n    dtype_regex = REGEX_INT\n    sampling_params.stop.extend([\" \", \"\\n\"])\nelif sampling_params.dtype in [\"float\", float]:\n    dtype_regex = REGEX_FLOAT\n    sampling_params.stop.extend([\" \", \"\\n\"])\n```\n\nHowever, `sgl.gen(..., stop=...)` accepts `Optional[Union[str, List[str]]]` (as well as tuples), and `StreamExecutor._resolve_sampling_params` copies `stop` as-is onto `SglSamplingParams`. Consequently:\n1. Calling `sgl.gen(\"val\", dtype=int, stop=\"\\n\")` or `sgl.gen(\"val\", dtype=float, stop=(\"\\n\", \";\"))` raises `AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'extend'` (or `'tuple' object has no attribute 'extend'`) inside the stream worker thread.\n2. Passing a `list` `stop` mutates the caller's list in place via `.extend([\" \", \"\\n\"])`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Normalize `sampling_params.stop` in `RuntimeEndpoint._handle_dtype_to_regex` (`[]` when falsy, `[sampling_params.stop]` when `isinstance(..., str)`, and `list(sampling_params.stop)` otherwise) before extending stop tokens for `int` and `float` dtypes.\n- Add CPU unit tests in `test/registered/unit/lang/test_runtime_endpoint_dtype.py`.\n\n## Prior Work & Credits\n- Credits to @merrymercy (Liangsheng Yin) for introducing `dtype`-constrained generation in `_handle_dtype_to_regex` (#1082, `a34dd86a7d`).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41098156247](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41098156247)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41098156319](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41098156319)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41098156502](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41098156502)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
